From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 07:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] techpack, qcacld: drop -Werror from the vendor Kbuilds

LineageOS builds these trees with the Android prebuilt Clang, which does not
diagnose what a current GCC does. Built with OpenEmbedded's aarch64 cross
toolchain they stop do_compile_kernelmodules outright, because each of these
25 Kbuilds appends a bare -Werror to its own cppflags and the vendor code is
full of warnings that compiler never emitted:

  techpack/audio/dsp/msm-dts-srs-tm-config.c:304   -Werror=misleading-indentation
  techpack/audio/asoc/sm6150.c:4189                -Werror=format=
  techpack/audio/asoc/msm-pcm-routing-v2.c:1147    -Werror=address
  drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/.../lim_send_sme_rsp_messages.c:824
      if ((&pMac->lim.gpSession[i] != NULL) && ...   -Werror=address

None of those is a defect this port introduced, and none is worth fixing at
the call site in a tree we do not own: the last one is testing whether the
address of an array element is NULL, which has been true-by-construction
since it was written.

Only the bare, unconditional -Werror token is removed, and only from vendor
directories (techpack/, drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0). Any -Werror=<specific>
form would be left alone - there are none in these files - and the warnings
themselves are unchanged and still printed. The kernel's own
CONFIG_CC_WERROR is handled separately, in the machine's luneos.cfg.

Same treatment as surya, whose tree needed it for the same reason, and as
mindphone before it (30 MediaTek vendor Makefiles).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor tree is built with Android's Clang]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
